# Check of the echo benchmark (TCP echo servers in C, Java and Erlang, benchmarks/echo/), with the real
# Scaphandre: every server as built and Erlang also with busy-waiting off (-nobw; C and Java have no such
# setting and are skipped), in Docker and natively. One connect test (one message per connection, clients
# 0.02 s apart), one burst and one stream: 24 measurements, about 30 min.
# Every row must have 0 failed messages, and Erlang -nobw must differ from Erlang as built only in ERL_FLAGS.
#   make run CONFIG=campaigns/check/echo.config
MACHINE=minimal
ENV_CPU_SPEED=1800
MEASURE=echo
VARIANTS=nobw:ERL_FLAGS=+sbwt none +sbwtdcpu none +sbwtdio none
DEPLOY=container native
REPEATS=1
IDLE_SECONDS=0
ECHO_CONNECT_CLIENTS=500
ECHO_CONNECT_SPACING_SECONDS=0.02
ECHO_BURST_CLIENTS=100
ECHO_BURST_MESSAGES=2000
ECHO_STREAM_CLIENTS=100
ECHO_STREAM_RATE_PER_SECOND=10
ECHO_STREAM_DURATION_SECONDS=10
ECHO_SIZES_BYTES=15
